From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Barnes <hello@jonbarnes.dev>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 17:35:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Only the frame's own picture is traced

Patch 0054 of the renderer series (OoT: Recompiled).

The user, 2026-10-09, of the pause menu's equipment page: "link has artifacting. maybe its using
link with ray tracing and its breaking", and only on that page.

The game draws the player's preview on that page into a picture of its own: a 64 by 112 color
image with a depth image of its own and a perspective view (Player_DrawPauseImpl), run from the
work list before the menu. Every test of a pair for tracing took it for the world: a perspective
projection, depth written. So the preview player was traced, lit by the frame's lights in a
picture a fifth of the frame's width.

A pair is now traced only when its color image is as wide as the widest of the workload's pairs,
which is the picture the frame is built in. Every pair the world is drawn in is that wide, so
nothing traced before is lost; a small picture the game renders for its own use is drawn as the
game drew it.

diff --git a/src/render/rt64_framebuffer_renderer.cpp b/src/render/rt64_framebuffer_renderer.cpp
--- a/src/render/rt64_framebuffer_renderer.cpp
+++ b/src/render/rt64_framebuffer_renderer.cpp
@@ -2400,6 +2400,20 @@ namespace RT64 {
         int32_t rtMainTransforms = -1;
         int32_t rtMainProj = -1;   // patch 0008: the projection itself, for its scissor and viewport
         uint32_t rtMainCalls = 0;
+
+        // ONLY THE FRAME'S OWN PICTURE IS TRACED (patch 0054). The game also draws into small
+        // pictures of its own, the player's preview on the pause menu's equipment page above all:
+        // a 64 by 112 color image with a depth image of its own and a perspective view, which every
+        // other test here takes for the world. Traced, the preview player was lit by the frame's
+        // lights in a picture a fifth of the frame's width ("link has artifacting", the user,
+        // 2026-10-09). A pair is traced only when its color image is as wide as the widest of the
+        // workload's pairs, which is the picture the frame is built in.
+        uint16_t widestColorImage = 0;
+        for (uint32_t fp = 0; fp < p.curWorkload->fbPairCount; fp++) {
+            widestColorImage = std::max(widestColorImage, p.curWorkload->fbPairs[fp].colorImage.width);
+        }
+        const bool framePicture = (fbPair.colorImage.width >= widestColorImage);
+
         if (p.rtEnabled) {
             for (uint32_t pr = 0; pr < fbPair.projectionCount; pr++) {
                 const Projection &candidate = fbPair.projections[pr];
@@ -2423,6 +2437,7 @@ namespace RT64 {
             // TODO: Use detected scenes logic instead.
             const bool perspProj = (proj.type == Projection::Type::Perspective);
             bool rtProj = p.rtEnabled && perspProj && fbPair.depthWrite && targetDrawCall.rtScenes.empty(); // TODO: Remove the last condition once multiple heaps per RT scene are supported.
+            rtProj = rtProj && framePicture;   // patch 0054
 
             // Only a projection that shares the main one's matrices starts or joins the traced
             // scene (patch 0003, see the choice above the loop).
